# Loaded automatically for every backend user because this package ships it as
# Configuration/user.tsconfig (core: TsConfigTreeBuilder, v14.3).
#
# A backend user's dashboards are created exactly once — on the first open of
# the module, and only while the user still has none at all
# (DashboardInitializationService::getDashboardsForUser). Which dashboards
# appear then comes from this setting, and EXT:dashboard defaults it to
# 'default' alone. Naming both presets from Configuration/Backend/DashboardPresets.php
# gives a new user the explainer dashboard AND the live-widget dashboard;
# without it the second one would have to be assembled by hand.
#
# Users that already exist are past that one-time branch, so they are served by
# the be_dashboards rows in data/seed-extensions.sql instead.
options.dashboard.dashboardPresetsForNewUsers = default,netresearch-widgets
